  "description": "Leinster Estates is pleased to present 3 Dillon Place South, Dublin 8, for short-term accommodation !! \n\nTaking Bookings for January - March 2027\n\n* Available:  4th January 2027\n* Min. stay:  4 weeks\n* Max. stay until: 28th March 2027\n* Rent includes broadband plus utilities (electricity, gas & refuse)\n\nTucked away on a quiet street just off Christchurch, this stylish ground-floor city pad puts you right in the heart of historic Dublin. The c.50 sqm end of terrace offers one bedroom, one bathroom, and a separate TV/reading room, and one exciting base for settling into the city for a month or two.\n\nThe location doesn't get any better for a short stay in Dublin. Temple Bar's pubs and live music scene are about a 10 minute walk, Grafton Street's shops and buskers are around 10 minutes, and Camden Street's restaurants and bars roughly the same distance again, 10-12 minutes away. History is on the doorstep too, with Christchurch Cathedral, Dublin Castle, Dublinia, and St Patrick's Cathedral all within easy reach on foot. For a taste of the real thing, the Teeling Whiskey Distillery in the Liberties is just a short stroll away, with the Guinness Storehouse not far beyond it.\n\nDublin is an energetic city that visitors can explore entirely on foot from here.  No transport schedules to plan around instead just historic streets to stroll, the best pubs, and Dublin's old history at every turn. There is of course public transport at your doorstep.  This is the kind of base that lets you live in the city rather than simply visit it. \n\nEarly enquiries are advised, as this well-located and stylish city pad will attract strong demand.  Please contact Stuart Ramke, Leinster Estates via e-mail for further information.",
